{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>You shall not be to him as a lender</b> — this is the one who lends. He says that you shall not be to him like a lender, who is like a ruler over the borrower, as it is written: \"and a borrower is a servant to the man who lends\" (Proverbs 22:7). Rather, you shall be to him in every respect as though he never borrowed from you at all, and you shall not impose interest upon him — that is, \"interest of silver, interest of food\" (Deuteronomy 23:20). Rather, the loan to him shall be an act of kindness; you shall take from him no benefit of honor and no benefit of money."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:14:18.262223730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}